<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Afon Mawddach</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as River Mawddach</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mawddach is a river of Gwynedd in north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> that flows from the hills north of Dolgellau into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardigan-bay">Cardigan Bay</a> at Barmouth through a wide, wooded estuary. The estuary is crossed by Barmouth Bridge, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> railway viaduct opened in 1867. In Welsh tradition the river marked a boundary of the early kingdom of Meirionnydd.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afon-mawddach.jpg" alt="Afon Mawddach" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Entopos · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mawddach_Estuary_from_above_Barmouth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
